#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""omarcal-helper — the omarcal backend.

Talks CalDAV directly over pooled HTTPS connections instead of going through
Evolution Data Server, so every request carries a real socket timeout and a
slow calendar degrades to an error on that calendar alone. Parsing, recurrence
expansion and VTIMEZONE handling come from libical (ICalGLib), a standalone
package that needs nothing from pip.

Every command prints one JSON object on stdout and exits 0; failures are
reported inside that object rather than by exit status, so the QML side always
has something to parse.

    login      --user U                  store a password, discover calendars
    calendars                            the calendar list and its state
    set-calendar --calendar C ...        colour / visibility / rename
    sync       [--calendar C] [--force]  incremental pull, all calendars at once
    events     --from ISO --to ISO       occurrences in a window
    event      --uid U [--rid R]         one event, every field
    search     --query Q [--limit N]     title/location/description match
    agenda     [--days N]                what is coming up
    status                               health, last sync, per-calendar errors
    settings   [--set k=v ...]           UI preferences
    watch      [--interval S]            refresh loop, one JSON line per change
"""

